    "created_at": "2019-09-13T14:17:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-13T14:17:41Z",
    "body": "The main reason for having `disabled` and `add_newline` is that the average user will want to only make a small change to Starship when using it. \r\nEg. Disable the `package` module or remove the `line_break`.\r\n\r\nThe `prompt_order` is easy to find if you are specifically looking to rearrange the prompt but is not intuitive to look for if you're trying to disable something specific.\r\n\r\nThe other drawback to having everyone use `prompt_order` to disable a specific module is that they won't be getting newly released modules between starship updates since the new modules aren't in their `prompt_order`.\r\n\r\nI'm open to rethinking our configuration, but I don't think solely using `prompt_order` would be the best option as it is.",
